    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for Ghost Ride the WHIP leans into high-leverage speed and favorable matchups against sub-par starters, headlined by **Brice Turang** (75.06) and **Corbin Carroll** (65.92). **Brice Turang** is our strongest play, benefiting from a soft matchup against Lowder (5.10 xERA) and an ideal spot in the three-hole, while **Corbin Carroll** remains a vital engine for our SB production despite the platoon disadvantage against Liberatore. **Tyler Soderstrom** (63.38) and **James Wood** (60.72) also represent core plays; **James Wood** is particularly intriguing, as his elite 0.404 xwOBA and aggressive positioning at the top of the order outweigh the moderate risk posed by Nola\u2019s strikeout profile.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Zach McKinstry**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a score of 47.70. While he benefits from a positive park factor and a platoon edge against Weathers, the overall output across our starting infield and utility spots proved more efficient, specifically when accounting for the negative weight of his #8 batting order position. We are exercising caution with **Seiya Suzuki** (49.16) and **Kyle Karros** (48.57), both of whom are hovering near our marginal floor; they remain in the lineup due to the lack of viable alternatives, but their sub-50 scores against Manaea and Suarez, respectively, bear watching.\n\nWe are actively monitoring a few high-risk profiles: **Jose Caballero** faces an uphill battle against the elite arm of Skubal (2.88 xERA), though his platoon advantage keeps him above water, and **Travis Bazzana** is seeing a significant drag on his score due to an unfavorable L/L matchup. Furthermore, our focus on SB efficiency means we are keeping a close eye on the catch-and-throw metrics of opposing backstops, as this has subtly depressed the projected scoring for **Max Muncy**, **James Wood**, and **Kyle Karros**. Should the weather report shift or official lineups force a change, we are prepared to pivot to the bench, though currently, our focus remains on maximizing the production of **Gabriel Moreno** and **Josh Naylor** against their respective right-handed opponents.",
